              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Doug Cutting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2008-03-31T18:55:50.906+0000",
          "updated": "2008-03-31T18:55:50.906+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12392738/comment/12583802",
          "id": "12583802",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "bq. Since the increment is relative to the prior token, it should make no difference when there is no prior token. So shouldn't the first token be at position=0 no matter what its increment?\n\nI'm ok with that ... but the other way to look at it is that there is a \"virtual token\" signifing the start of the Field, and the first physical tokens increment is relative that ... with things like SpanFirstQueries not allowing the \"first\" token to specify an arbitrary increment from the 'virtual\" start of the field has real consequences.\n\n(consider an Analyzer that only indexes proper names and wants to record real positions so that a SpanFirstQuery can find docs where Doug Cutting appears in the first 100 Tokens)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
